# Adapters ship as executable scripts and CI configs installed directly into
# other projects' .git/hooks/ or .github/workflows/. A CRLF line ending breaks
# a shebang line on Linux/CI even though the file still "looks fine" on
# Windows editors. Force LF for everything under Adapters/, regardless of the
# checkout platform or user's core.autocrlf setting.
/Adapters/** text eol=lf

# Registry/ is parsed by those same shell consumers with grep and sed (see
# Registry/README.md's parsing contract). A CRLF checkout would leave a
# trailing carriage return on every extracted Employee name, so `grep -qxF`
# would match nothing and the commit-msg hook would reject every valid
# Employee. The consumers strip \r defensively as well, but the file itself
# must not be the thing that introduces it.
/Registry/** text eol=lf

# .github/ holds this repository's own installed copies of the Adapters above,
# and the yaml-lint job compares them against the Adapters/ originals. Keeping
# both sides LF means a diff between them reflects real content drift rather
# than a line-ending difference on a Windows checkout.
/.github/** text eol=lf
